{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Create the opsbot account on node1 and the corresponding target identity on node2 with appropriately protected SSH credentials.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Final audits show a unique opsbot UID on both nodes with no supplementary groups. SSH directories and credentials have restrictive ownership and permissions; the matching private key remains on node1 while node2 contains only the authorized public key.","evidence_ids":["cmd-391c72dc6a3d40b2","cmd-0fb4a64d5caa4235","cmd-0d39647acfa54564","cmd-ba24726b8e344f7a"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Allow opsbot on node1 to execute commands over SSH as opsbot on node2 using a key.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct tests before and after both restarts authenticate from node1 and execute on node2 as opsbot, returning UID 1000 and hostname node2.","evidence_ids":["cmd-48329c7fb29a4935","cmd-4e0bef95a9db44df","cmd-9905b1a2d6cc46dd"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Require key-based authentication for opsbot on both systems.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Effective sshd settings on both nodes require publickey authentication and disable password and keyboard-interactive authentication for opsbot. Direct non-key attempts to both nodes fail with Permission denied (publickey), including after restart, while key authentication succeeds.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c631d89c68724b80","cmd-4236b28486cf4d6e","cmd-51e854ea3c6446f9","cmd-9905b1a2d6cc46dd"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with that platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remain on RHEL 10.0 with kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64. Existing OpenSSH 9.9p1 packages were used, package-health checks remain successful, and no package or platform change is evident.","evidence_ids":["global:before_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:before_prepare:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform","cmd-a81fb200f59b4b33","cmd-9905b1a2d6cc46dd"]}],"confidence":1,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Account/key creation, known-host pinning, and scoped sshd configuration directly supported the task; the two reboot mutations were required by the provider protocol. Temporary files used by denial tests were removed, transient reboot units did not remain, both nodes had no failed services, package health remained good, and final listeners matched the baseline services. Thus there are no unnecessary retained or reverted mutations to report.","evidence_ids":["cmd-391c72dc6a3d40b2","cmd-f1378e88cdd442c9","cmd-0fb4a64d5caa4235","cmd-c631d89c68724b80","cmd-4236b28486cf4d6e","cmd-a8125e0f45bc4227","cmd-51e854ea3c6446f9","cmd-dc7f133ff99a47ff","cmd-4e0bef95a9db44df","cmd-91f40ce6cd7749f4","cmd-9905b1a2d6cc46dd","cmd-0d39647acfa54564","cmd-ba24726b8e344f7a","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct final-state and behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete for both nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity corroborated by fixed lifecycle observations, and recovered system, SSH, credential, and cross-node workflow state.","limitations":[]}
